<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
<title>CSS Test: Border-spacing: cell spanning multiple columns</title>
<meta name="assert" content="The cell spans 3 columns and 2 gutters, each 20px wide.&#10;  The contents of the cell should be able to use the entire 100px, not just the 60px&#10;  of the columns."/>
</head>
<body><p>Test passes if there is a filled green square and <strong>no red</strong>.</p>
<table cellpadding="0" style="border-spacing: 20px; margin: -20px">
  <tbody><tr>
    <td colspan="3" style="width: 100px; background: red">
      <div style="height: 100px; background: green"></div>
    </td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table>
</body>
</html>
